import json, html
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];out=root/'output/kernel_optimized';data=json.loads((out/'results.json').read_text());rows=data['records'];h=data['hardware']
lines=['Optimized whole-tree benchmark',h['cpu']+' / '+h['gpu'],h['timing'],f"Julia {h['julia']}, {h['threads']} Julia thread, {h['blas_threads']} BLAS thread, {h['precision']} statistics.",'']
body='<h1>Scheduled kernel tree performance</h1><p>'+html.escape(lines[1])+'</p><p>'+html.escape(lines[2])+'</p><p>Same seeds, cuts, arrival order within each region, and compression settings. Planning, input transfers, state transfers and final model construction are included. Small workloads use five timed repetitions; larger ones use three. Trial order is rotated. Other workstation applications may affect timings.</p><table><tr><th>Workload</th><th>Backend</th><th>Median seconds</th><th>Range</th><th>Posts/s</th><th>Speedup vs original</th><th>Leaves</th></tr>'
for r in rows:
    times=[s['seconds'] for s in r['samples']]
    values=[r['case'],r['method'],f"{r['median_seconds']:.5f}",f'{min(times):.5f}–{max(times):.5f}',f"{r['posts_per_second']:,.0f}",f"{r['speedup']:.2f}×",r['leaves']]
    body+='<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+html.escape(str(v))+'</td>' for v in values)+'</tr>';lines.append(' | '.join(str(v) for v in values))
body+='</table>'
worst={key:max(s[key] for r in rows for s in r['samples']) for key in ['probability_tv','max_mean_error','max_covariance_error']}
lines+=['',f'Identical topology and reservoirs asserted in every measured fit. Worst errors: {worst}', 'Scheduled execution uses the original topology rules and computes each region in causal order; it fits a supplied batch. Per-post callback and external eigensolver modes retain the event driver.']
body+='<h2>Correctness</h2><p>Every fit asserts identical topology and reservoir contents and checks probabilities, means and covariances against the original. Worst errors: '+html.escape(str(worst))+'.</p><h2>What changed</h2><p>Cut locations depend on reservoir geometry and arrival counts, so they can be planned without PPCA updates. The numerical pass then processes regions in dependency order, preserving each region’s observation order and transferring moments before its children run. Buffers persist between launches; each tree level exchanges packed state. Cooperating GPU threads handle embedding coordinates, with a register-based 2D specialization.</p><p>This is the optimized whole-batch fit API. Intermediate callbacks and custom external eigensolvers still use the original event driver; those modes are not represented by these speedups. No cut thresholds, ranks or decay parameters were relaxed. Model statistics remain Float64. No claim is made that every possible stream is faster.</p><p><a href="results.json">Raw trials and settings</a> · <a href="summary.txt">Summary</a> · <a href="run.log">Run log</a></p>'
(out/'summary.txt').write_text('\n'.join(lines));(out/'demo.html').write_text('<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Optimized kernel tree speed</title><style>body{max-width:1450px;margin:30px auto;padding:20px;font:16px system-ui;background:#111827;color:#eee}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:12px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #475569}a{color:#7dd3fc}</style>'+body)
print('\n'.join(lines))
